# Help: KVM arm64's optional parts: PMU, pointer auth, EL2 tracing, ptdump
#
# Layered on virt/kvm-arm64.config: PMU emulation over the ARM PMU
# framework, pointer authentication for guests, the nVHE hypervisor's
# tracing and list checks, and the stage-2 page table dump in debugfs.
# Most default to y, which an allnoconfig-based merge drops.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - virt/kvm-arm64.config's KVM, under which the options below sit.
# - PERF_EVENTS=y + ARM_PMU=y turn on HW_PERF_EVENTS, which has no
#   prompt.
# - NVHE_EL2_DEBUG=y, the nVHE hypervisor's debug mode, which BUG()s
#   on a failure report, FTRACE=y and a tracer, FUNCTION_TRACER, turn
#   on NVHE_EL2_TRACING, which has no prompt; Linux 7.3 also asks for
#   the TRACING the tracer selects.
# - DEBUG_KERNEL=y + DEBUG_FS=y gate PTDUMP_STAGE2_DEBUGFS.
#
# Every symbol is bool. No builtin/ counterpart needed.
# See: arch/arm64/kvm/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/virt/kvm/arm/index.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION=y
CONFIG_KVM=y
CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y
CONFIG_ARM_PMU=y
CONFIG_FTRACE=y
CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER=y
CONFIG_NVHE_EL2_DEBUG=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y

#
# KVM features
#
CONFIG_ARM64_PTR_AUTH=y
CONFIG_LIST_HARDENED=y
CONFIG_NVHE_EL2_TRACING=y
CONFIG_PTDUMP_STAGE2_DEBUGFS=y
